# charon integration step 21 after 546078ea5d: commit ac36b347d2d19dedcac134e731ff06b75031c945
# first parent dc811b035115954da6c1db36a7c4f12b9d23bbd0
# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: generate-ml decodes opaque fields that contain hash-consed values
#
# The Rust serializer deduplicates Ty and TraitRef values across the whole file:
# the first occurrence carries the value and its key, later ones only the key.
# The generated OCaml decoder skipped #[charon::opaque] fields without decoding
# them, so keys first defined inside such a field were never registered and a
# later {"Deduplicated": k} failed with 'Hash-consing key not found'.
#
# TraitAssocTyImpl.implied_trait_refs is such a field. Its doc claimed it is
# empty after lift_associated_item_clauses, but that pass only lifts clauses of
# non-generic associated types; GATs such as Pattern::Searcher<'a> keep them
# (e.g. the Searcher<'a> bound of impl Pattern for &str, reached from
# str::starts_with).
#
# generate-ml now decodes, and discards, every opaque field whose type can reach
# HashConsed; other opaque fields (Binder.kind, Body.comments) stay skipped. The
# OCaml types are unchanged. Fix the doc comment. The ml-gat-implied-trait-refs
# ui test emits a deduplicated llbc that the charon-ml deserialization test
# loads.

